# Todero — Cursor Rules

You are working on Todero, an AI-run company OS built with Next.js 14 + Supabase + TypeScript.

## Read First
1. `./CLAUDE.md` — Project tech stack, build rules, MC API spec, layout integrity
2. `./AGENTS.md` — Runtime-neutral agent system, portability flags, pipeline rules
3. `~/kaos-config/SOUL.md` — Behavioral rules (direct, no filler, have opinions)
4. `~/kaos-config/AGENTS.md` — Issue lifecycle, git rules, workflow protocols
5. `~/kaos-config/self-improving/memory.md` — Accumulated lessons (HOT tier)

## Project Stack
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router
- Language: TypeScript strict mode
- Database: Supabase (Postgres) — service role key in env
- Styling: Tailwind CSS with design tokens
- Deploy: LaunchAgent `com.nabit.todero` → `localhost:3000` → Cloudflare tunnel → https://kaos.nabit.work

## Non-Negotiable Rules
1. All issue state changes go through `POST/PATCH /api/issues` — never direct Supabase
2. Required fields for `in_review`: `implementation_notes`, `commit_sha`, `regression_test`
3. Never `git push` from an agent session — KAOS batches PRs at 7am/7pm ET
4. Never `gh pr create`, `gh pr merge`, `gh pr close`, `gh pr edit`, `gh pr review`
5. 200-line component limit — extract to `components/tabs/`
6. Commit format: `feat(TASK-KEY): description [skip ci]`
7. `trash` > `rm` for destructive operations
8. Run `npm run build` before committing — zero TypeScript errors required

## Layout Integrity (MC-175) — do not break
| Element | Required class |
|---|---|
| Desktop sidebar | `hidden md:flex` |
| Mobile bottom nav | `lg:hidden fixed bottom-0` |
| Hamburger button | `md:hidden` |
| Mobile more menu | `lg:hidden fixed bottom-[56px]` |

## Runtime
This project uses a pluggable runtime adapter (`lib/runtimes/`). When you add
a new agent behavior, keep the runtime assumption neutral: your code should
work whether the underlying LLM is Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor.
